  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding growth of compounded interest</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>An account is opened with an initial deposit of \(\text{N\$ }{@principal@} \) and earns 
\({@rate@}\%\) interest compounded semi-annually.</p>
<p>What will be the account worth in \({@years@}\) years.</p>
<p>Amount \(= \text{N\$ } \)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Amount is calculated using the formula;</p>
<p>\(A=P(1+\displaystyle \frac{r}{n})^{\text{nt}}\)</p>
<p>where,</p>
<p> A= amount=?</p>
<p> P = principal= \({@principal@}\)</p>
<p>r = rate of interest=\({@rate_float@}\)</p>
<p>n = number of times interest is compounded per year=semi-annaully</p>
<p>t = time (in years)\(={@years@}\)</p>

<p>Substituting values to the formula we have</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
A&=P(1+\displaystyle \frac{r}{n})^{\text{nt}}\\
&={@principal@}\left (1+\displaystyle \frac{{@rate_float@}}{{@2@}}\right )^{2({@years@})}\\
&={@principal@}\left (1+{@rate_float/2@}\right )^{2({@years@})}\\
&={@principal@}({@sol1@})\\
&={@ta1@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
